#: ae5ffe86655d462e8ab4473ff1069f9a
msgid "For any model-specific hardware requirements, see the relevant model's `Datasheet <https://www.vectornav.com/resources/technical-documentation/datasheets>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:40
#: 7913c3ab3f554326aecb437e06a1c09b
msgid "Mounting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:41
#: fbbda0404fa04a4495317a45293c8efa
msgid "The VectorNav sensor can be mounted in any orientation, in any position on the vehicle, without regard to center of gravity. All VectorNav sensors default to a coordinate system of x-forward, y-right, and z-down, making the default mounting as connector-back, base-down. This can be changed to any rigid rotation using the VectorNav Reference Frame Rotation register."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:43
#: 87cc0777fde54157a66b689e3eb61490
msgid "If using a GNSS-enabled product, the GNSS antenna must be mounted rigidly with respect to the inertial sensor and with an unobstructed sky view. If using a dual-GNSS-enabled product (VN-3X0), the secondary antenna must be mounted rigidly with respect to the primary antenna and the inertial sensor with an unobstructed sky view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:45
#: cbda3f940aee463fab91074a0d5c4f03
msgid "For more mounting requirements and recommendations, see the relevant model's `Quick Start Guide <https://www.vectornav.com/resources/technical-documentation/quick-start-guides>`__ and `User Manual <https://www.vectornav.com/resources/technical-documentation/user-manuals>`__."
msgstr ""

