#: 577872eca2334585934d740d2422e137
msgid "There are two possible ways for VectorNav data to be used by ArduPilot: as an external sensor set to ArduPilot's EKFs or as an external AHRS. Both ways utilize ArduPilot's External AHRS driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:154
#: af1ea7c88a9448849e52f9200fdabbf6
msgid "To establish communication with the VectorNav unit, set the following for the relevant serial port:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:156
#: 288a5ce18c5f4e539216c4c240cdde0a
msgid "``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` = 36 (AHRS)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:157
#: 7883af10b7934926b2cdbd323c7bd793
msgid "``SERIALx_BAUD`` = matching VectorNav sensor baudrate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:160
#: 7a39ce2480654d3eb397fe83109bc4c4
msgid "The External AHRS-specific parameters may not be visible before the ``Serialx_Protocol`` parameter is configured. As such, either a Refresh Params or a reset of ArduPilot may be necessary to see the parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:163
#: 56b39c7523bd48e396332784bbba8efb
msgid "Use as an External Sensor Set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:164
#: ce4eb8d456e14154931176ec99d55798
msgid "If set up as an external sensor, VectorNav's raw sensor data (IMU, GNSS, Compass, Barometer, and GNSS, if available) can be used by ArduPilot's internal EKFs, as configured. After the serial parameters have been configured, configure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:166
#: 142c29b83cbd49b9a5c21f8c04519898
msgid ":ref:`AHRS_EKF_TYPE<AHRS_EKF_TYPE>` = 3 (ArduPilot’s EKF3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:167
#: abb6378566234bafb1f648d3f1092388
msgid ":ref:`EAHRS_TYPE<EAHRS_TYPE>` = 1 (VectorNav)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:168
#: 3b514982da234a9fa5676b9fecb57dd2
msgid ":ref:`EAHRS_OPTIONS<EAHRS_OPTIONS>` bit 0 set to \"1\" value to disable ArduPilot's use of the bias-compensated IMU data, letting ArduPilot's filters do that (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:169
#: 187001831c1b4bab891c2e3cd2169bc1
msgid ":ref:`GPS1_TYPE<GPS1_TYPE>` = 21 (External AHRS) (If using a GNSS-enabled unit)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:170
#: edb35acb2a73450eab0ec63050089054
msgid ":ref:`GPS2_TYPE<GPS2_TYPE>` = 21 (External AHRS) (If using a Dual GNSS-enabled unit)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:172
#: 58551c79ca31434d8113bb7e638b7501
msgid "If desired, :ref:`EAHRS_SENSORS<EAHRS_SENSORS>` may be used to specify which sensor data should be used by ArduPilot's filters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:174
#: 61c9709068d94e28b0862b9457b3a9f0
msgid "Because ArduPilot's internal EKF will only update at the input IMU rate, it is recommended to raise the VectorNav IMU output rate beyond the default 50Hz. To do so, set :ref:`EAHRS_RATE<EAHRS_RATE>` to the desired IMU rate (800Hz maximum, 400Hz maximum for VN-300). Because the IMU output rate is configured on initialization, an ArduPilot reset is required after changing :ref:`EAHRS_RATE<EAHRS_RATE>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:177
#: 0ae0fae3b3c54b959e73ceabd64870ef
msgid "Use as an External AHRS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:178
#: 854b383bf57d4bd086d2745dbe75dc7d
msgid "Configuring ArduPilot to use the VectorNav sensor as an External AHRS will use the VectorNav PVTA (position, velocity, time, and attitude) solution as canonical rather than one of the possible internal ArduPilot filters. This will allow ArduPilot to use the VectorNav sensor's INS data that combines IMU and GNSS data in an advanced Kalman filtering estimation to provide position, velocity, and attitude estimates of higher accuracies and with better dynamic performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-vectornav.rst:182
#: b639d034abf345618736e77073700365
msgid "VectorNav uses the term AHRS to refer to an attitude-only solution, without absolute position measurement input. VectorNav uses the term INS to refer to a solution which accepts a position (often GNSS) measurement input and outputs a full PVTA. Because ArduPilot's External AHRS driver requires the data source (VectorNav) to provide an absolute PVT, use as an External AHRS is restricted to a VectorNav INS-enabled product (VN-2X0 or VN-3X0)."
msgstr ""

